!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-record-fields-value-read-against-a-sibling-reference-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    The kernel's `record_field.value` is typed `type!`, and `record_field.type` may hold a sibling reference, which
    names no type. Where `value` is absent nothing is read against `type`; where one is written, as here, the sibling
    names no type a value can be read against, and the field is refused naming `type`. This is what keeps the kernel's
    own dependent field sound.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
